  "additional_changes_made_in_scope": [
    "EVASION PATHS THE BASH DETECTION DOES NOT COVER — recorded here because the brief asked for them explicitly, and stated just as prominently in the script header under 'LIMITATIONS — READ BEFORE TRUSTING'. Bash guarding is BEST-EFFORT, NOT A SANDBOX; it raises the cost of an ACCIDENTAL violation and does not stop a determined one. Known unclosed evasions: (1) variable indirection — `D=src; printf x > \"$D/lib.rs\"`; (2) decoded or constructed commands — `base64 -d <<<... | sh`, `eval \"$(...)\"`; (3) command substitution in the target — `printf x > \"$(printf src/lib.rs)\"`; (4) writing through a helper — ./my-writer.sh, make, a cargo build script, any program the hook sees only by name; (5) `git apply` / `patch` — the PATCH BODY is never inspected, so a diff touching src/** passes unless a protected path appears in argv; (6) quoted paths containing spaces are tokenized naively (`read -ra` on whitespace), so `> \"src/my file.rs\"` yields the token `\"src/my` which still normalizes to a `src` segment and denies, but the reverse case — an allowed path containing a space — could mis-split; (7) `;` `|` `&&` INSIDE a quoted string split the command incorrectly (the splitter is textual, not a shell parser), which can both over- and under-block; (8) MultiEdit and NotebookEdit are NOT covered — only Edit, Write and Bash, per the brief's explicit three-tool scope. (8) is a named Phase-2 gap rather than a silent scope change; MultiEdit in particular carries file_path and would be a one-line addition if the reviewer wants it now.",
    "ACCEPTED OVER-BLOCK, documented in the header: because segment matching runs over the WHOLE normalized path, a path whose ancestor directory is literally named src/engine/tests OUTSIDE this repo (the common `~/src/notes.md` shape) is denied for a guarded seat. Deliberate: guarded seats work inside the repo, over-blocking is the safe direction for a guard whose purpose is stopping source writes, and the deny reason names the path so a human can see instantly what happened. The alternative (anchoring to $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR) would have broken the brief's requirement that the guard work for paths inside ANY worktree.",
    "NOTE ON `engine/**`, following the observation ASH-A already recorded in its own output.json: `engine/**` is a CONCEPTUAL path — the engine crate physically lives at src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine and is therefore already covered by the `src` segment rule. The hook implements a literal `engine` segment anyway, so both the conceptual and any future real engine/ tree are covered. Arms 10, 19 and 21 use literal engine/ paths.",
    "scripts/agent-test.sh ABORTS EARLY on a known-red fixture, so its aggregate exit is vacuous and the new `test-seat-path-guard` arm may never be reached in an aggregate run. Per the brief I did NOT run agent-test.sh in aggregate. The suite is fully runnable standalone (`bash scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh`) and that is how it was verified, including from an unrelated cwd to prove SCRIPT_DIR/REPO_ROOT resolution.",
    "The suite grew from the brief's 16 required arms to 55 assertions across 43 numbered arms. All 16 required arms are present with their required verdicts. The additions are: the four hook-shape assertions (exists / executable / bash shebang / fail-open EXIT trap present); one Bash write-verb arm each for tee, cp, mv, rm, dd of=, git checkout --, git restore, inline python3 -c, inline node -e, truncate; absolute-path-in-another-worktree; `..` traversal laundering; four extra false-positive guards; unhandled-tool; non-guarded agent_type; both directions of env-vs-payload precedence; the spawned-subagent shape (agent_id + agent_type together); case/whitespace tolerance; and two stderr-silence arms. Three malformed-input sub-arms were added to arm 12 (JSON with no tool_input, valid JSON of the wrong shape, empty stdin).",
    "NOTHING ON THE DO-NOT-TOUCH LIST WAS MODIFIED. Verified by `git status --short` at the end: the only changed paths in this slice are .claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh (new), .gitignore, scripts/agent-test.sh, scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh, and this output.json. In particular: .claude/settings.json is UNMODIFIED (it is not even present in this worktree, and the hook ships unwired); dev/todos-and-considerations-ledger.jsonl and its .seq were never read-modify-written, appended, or staged; dev/steward/steward-ledger.jsonl was not touched; .claude/agents/implementer.md and every `tools:` frontmatter line are byte-identical to baseline; no file under src/ or engine/ and no existing test source was touched; dev/design/orchestration.md, AGENTS.md, .claude/agents/orchestrator.md and .claude/agents/steward.md are untouched (ASH-A's, left alone); the 0.8.20 plan/board/release-state and src/conformance/governed-surface-allowlist.json are untouched. No worktree was created, moved or removed; nothing was pushed; no maturin develop / pip install -e was run.",
    "FIX-1 SCOPE DISCIPLINE. Exactly the three permitted files were touched across the two fix-1 commits: .claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh, scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh, and this output.json. `git status --porcelain` before the GREEN commit listed those two code files and nothing else. The DO-NOT-TOUCH list holds: .claude/settings.json is still UNTOUCHED and still UNTRACKED (`git ls-files | grep -c 'claude/settings'` = 0), so THE HOOK REMAINS UNWIRED and suite arm 16 still passes against the primary checkout's real settings.json and settings.local.json; .claude/agents/*.md and every `tools:` frontmatter line, both ledgers and the .seq, the 0.8.20 plan/board/release-state, src/conformance/governed-surface-allowlist.json, dev/design/orchestration.md, AGENTS.md, and ASH-A's already-reviewed .gitignore and scripts/agent-test.sh hunks were all left alone. No worktree was created, moved or removed; no landed commit was rewritten; nothing was pushed.",
