## Verdict: CONCERN

### 1. [medium] `sed -i -f - src/...` is a new false negative
Refs: [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:344), [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:373), [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:381), [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:399), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:614)

While waiting for the `-f`/`--file` program operand, the branch treats any `-...` token as “a flag, not the program” and keeps searching. For valid `sed -i -f - src/rust/lib.rs` or `sed -i --file - src/rust/lib.rs`, the `-` means “read the script from stdin”, but the hook skips it, then skips `src/rust/lib.rs` as the “first bare operand” program, so no protected file operand is ever considered. That is exactly the dangerous direction the fix was supposed to avoid, so D1 is not fully closed.

### 2. [low] The redirection header still is not exact about what the suite proves
Refs: [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:296), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:653)

The runtime `>|` fix looks correct, but the header says the listed redirection forms are “each verified by an arm” and includes `&>>`. Arms `56e/56f` cover `&>` only; there is no `&>>` arm in 44-56. That is a doc/test exactness mismatch, not a behavior hole, but this round was explicitly trying to eliminate that class of drift.

## What passed on inspection
- The implementer’s correction on the original D1 witness is right. With segment-based matching, `sed -i 's#src/rust/lib.rs#x#' ...` does not produce a bare `src` segment, while arms 47-50 do target real pre-fix mechanisms: [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:177), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:549).
- D2 itself is closed. `scan_bash_command` now folds `>|` to `>` before splitting on `|`, so glued, spaced, and `2>|` forms reach the redirection matcher: [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:491), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:626).
- `absorb_quoted_word` is bounded by token count and I did not find an infinite-loop path. It correctly preserves the intended `'\''` and double-quoted-apostrophe cases covered by 50b/50c: [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:257), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:593).
- The pre-fix guard behavior still holds in the current code: only `orchestrator|steward` are guarded, `implementer` stays untouched, only `Edit|Write|Bash` are handled, heredoc bodies are stripped, test-source precedence still wins, and allow paths stay silent/fail-open: [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:125), [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:177), [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:227), [seat-path-guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/hooks/seat-path-guard.sh:603), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:202), [test_seat_path_guard.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/scripts/tests/test_seat_path_guard.sh:451).
- The hook is still unwired in the settings I could read, and `implementer.md`’s frontmatter is unchanged in the current tree: [settings.json](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/.claude/settings.json:52), [implementer.md](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/agent-seat-hardening/.claude/agents/implementer.md:4).

